# ── Secrets — never commit ─────────────────────────────
# Per-board provisioning (copied from the Tollan console bundle + WiFi creds).
# Matched at any depth: the bundle's own tollan_config.h holds a one-time
# enrollment token that can enrol a board as your device.
tollan_config.h
secrets.h
sensors.json

# Certs / keys anywhere in the tree
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx

# ── Downloaded Tollan bundles ──────────────────────────
# The bundle archive and its extracted form both carry the enrollment token
# and the device identity. Keep them out of git.
tollan-esp32-sensor/
tollan-esp32-sensor-*/
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# ── Vendored third-party (TollanAgent) ──────────────────
# The TollanAgent library is proprietary: it ships inside your ESP32 device
# bundle and is "licensed only for use with the Tollan service"
# (docs.tollan.ie/esp32-getting-started.html). Download it from your bundle
# and unzip it here — do NOT commit it. lib/README.md is tracked on purpose.
lib/TollanAgent/
lib/tollan-agent/
lib/tollan-agent-library/

# The 0.1.0 source fork of TollanAgent, kept for reference only (it has a
# 4 KB frame buffer the shipped build does not). Lives outside lib/ so the
# Library Dependency Finder does not pick it up alongside the real library.
legacy/

# ── Local agent memory / daemon state ──────────────────
# Machine-local: contains absolute paths, PIDs and a local SQLite db.
.graymatter/

# ── PlatformIO ─────────────────────────────────────────
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
build/
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake

# ── Python (poller-side helpers, if any) ───────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.env

# ── VS Code ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep extensions.json (shared recommendations), ignore
# auto-generated / machine-local files with absolute paths.
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/ipch/

# ── OS / editor junk ───────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
